## Status

Accepted

## Context

We were keeping track of the number of checks we had made on the site using the `num_checks` variable, which was initialized at the beginning of the `page_load.js` file:

```js
let num_checks = 0;
```

The number of checks was also being increased by `count_checks_function` in the `page_load.js` file:

```js
function count_checks_function() {
  num_checks++;
  if (num_checks < 1000) {
    num_checks = Math.max(0, num_checks); // keep it positive
    document.querySelector("div#bot_page_load_status span#bot_page_load_total_checks").textContent = `Checks completed: ${num_checks}`;
  }
}
```

The `count_checks_function` was run whenever a new page was loaded, which triggered the increment of `num_checks` and re-rendering of the page, which was used by the `bot_page_load_status` div to render the current status of the page load.

