## Status

Accepted

## Context

There is a need to support custom key-value properties, like `color` and `size` for the data source within the storage plugin.

## Decision

As there are no plans to add this feature to a storage plugin in the near future, support custom properties is implemented as a workaround to support custom properties on-the-fly.

Custom properties are managed within the storage plugin, and every call to `save` and `get` within the storage plugin will be validated for custom properties (unless only the data within the storage plugin is fetched), and if supported by the storage plugin, they are added to the custom properties, which are then used to validate the data format within the storage plugin.

## Consequences

This ensures that if custom properties exist, they are also used to validate and generate the metadata used when saving the data.

Custom properties may not be generated using the default value when a property is added to the storage plugin, and if an custom property is added to the storage plugin with a default value and is used during a save/get operation, the default value will be added to the custom properties.

To add custom properties to a storage plugin, the storage plugin will have to be added to the registry within a key set, and when the storage plugin is added, a custom property will be added to the storage plugin.

To retrieve the custom properties for a storage plugin, `getCustomProperties()` will be called on the storage plugin and returns an array of custom properties, for example:

```js
const customProperties = storagePlugin.getCustomProperties();
// customProperties will be an array of properties with names and types. For example:
// customProperties: [
//   { name: 'color', type: 'string' },
//   { name: 'size', type: 'number' }
// ]
```

To retrieve custom properties specific to a custom property name, `customProperties.get('color')` will be used to retrieve the value of the `color` custom property, and in this case `color` is a string.

The `getCustomProperties()` method will be called inside `getValue()` and `keySetBase()` to ensure that custom properties are passed into the storage plugin.

When adding custom properties to the storage plugin, the `color` and `size` properties are added to the storage plugin, so that for all subsequent saves, custom properties are added to the storage plugin.

`getCustomProperties()` returns all custom properties added to the storage plugin, which will be an array of custom properties, for example:

```js
const customProperties = storagePlugin.getCustomProperties();
// customProperties will be an array of properties with names and types. For example:
// customProperties: [
//   { name: 'color', type: 'string' },
//   { name: 'size', type: 'number' }
// ]
```

Custom properties will only be available inside the storage plugin, and may not be added to the saved data, or back into the storage plugin.

