```

Deprecate with opt-out functionality solves a number of the previous issue's:

- When an inactive feature is being referenced, the reference will be marked as deprecated and the reference may have changed.
- When the inactive feature receives bug fixes, these bug fixes will be shared for the inactive feature because it is no longer considered a beta feature.
- When the inactive feature is eventually removed, all references to the inactive feature (including unused inactive features) are removed from the `app-main` version.

We can deprecate a feature with opt-out functionality once the `app-main` release is in beta and then the deprecation is only temporary until the release drops out of beta.

