This would mean that the code around the deprecated feature is modified to read from the `app-main` version and then the feature is eventually removed from the `app-main` version, after which no more bug-fixes are added to the feature.

Deprecate without opt-out functionality is an easier solution than deprecate with opt-out functionality because it can be implemented immediately when an inactive feature is encountered.
